464 - When I Can Read My Title Clear
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 464
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[D]When I can [G]read my title [Am]clear
[G/B]To mansions in the skies
[G]I'll bid farewell [C]to every fear,
[Em]And wipe my weeping eyes;
[Bm]And wipe my weeping eyes,
[G]And wipe my [C]weeping eyes,
[C/E]I'll bid farewell [G/D]to every fear,
[G/D]And wipe my [D]weeping eyes.

Verse 2:
[D]Should earth against [G]my soul [Am]engage,
[G/B]And fiery darts be hurled,
[G]Then I can smile [C]at Satan's rage,
[Em]And face a frowning world;
[Bm]And face a frowning world,
[G]And face a [C]frowning world,
[C/E]Then I can [G/D]smile at Satan's rage,
[G/D]And face a [D]frowning world.

Verse 3:
[D]Let cares [G]like a wild [Am]deluge come,
[G/B]And storms or sorrow fall!
[G]May I but safely [C]reach my home,
[Em]May God, my heav'n, my all;
[Bm]My God. my heav'n, my all,
[G]My God, my [C]heav'n, my all,
[C/E]May I but [G/D]safely reach my home,
[G/D]My God, my [D]heav'n, my all.
